# What Vercel uploads and builds. The deployment is api/*.py plus public/, and the only dependency
# any of it has is python-chess, which requirements.txt pins.
#
# pyproject.toml and uv.lock are excluded on purpose. They exist for local development and for
# parity with the competition platform, which preinstalls torch, numba, onnxruntime and numpy.
# Vercel's Python builder reads them in preference to requirements.txt and installs the lot, which
# came to 337 MB per function and 1011 MB across the three routes, against a 500 MB cap. Nothing
# reachable from a request imports any of those four: agent.py and every module under api/ need
# python-chess and the standard library, and nothing else.
pyproject.toml
uv.lock

# Local tooling and the competition harness. No request path reaches any of it.
harness/
baselines/
tools/
docs/
.github/
Makefile
submission.zip

# Prose, not code.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
DEVELOPMENT.md
README.md

# Local artefacts.
.venv/
__pycache__/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
games/
*.pgn
